LLM DIAGNOSTIC DECISION TREE

1) MCP TOOL FAILED TO RUN
  Is mcpd running? Run tools/list; all eight tools are always available.
  Is the command noninteractive and <3 seconds?
  Are all six process slots occupied? ps on console.

2) COMMAND RETURNS usage:
  Run help COMMAND. Most PicoNIX commands have fewer switches
  than GNU equivalents; grep has no -i and no regex mode.

3) FILE NOT FOUND / CANNOT OPEN
  ls /tmp ; ls /man ; pwd
  Ensure program is in /bin or RAM file exists.
  /proc, /man, /dev and /tmp have different semantics.

4) C/ASM BUILD FAILED
  get_manual(topic='languages/c') and get_manual(topic='c-debug')
  Check output filename /tmp/foo.s, source size, Thumb-1 forms.
  'cc' success is NOT an executable until 'as' succeeds.

5) PYTHON PROGRAM FAILED
  get_manual(topic='languages/python') and get_manual(topic='python-debug')
  Remove CPython-only imports, methods, defs or classes.
  Check 16 vars, 64 lines, 2048 source bytes, pool limit.

6) APPLICATION RUNS BUT NOT EXPECTED RESULT
  Check input/result sizes and return values; trace on -s,
  execute one short operation; trace show, then trace on.
  Inspect ps/lsof and bounded memory.

7) NETWORK / MCP STREAM INTERRUPTED
  HTTP incomplete chunked read is transport incomplete, not
  necessarily command abort. Reconnect, inspect state, and only
  repeat safe reads. For large output use smaller chunks.

8) DEVICE DID NOT RESPOND
  Check pins, supply/wiring, I2C address, PWM channel and
  shared frequency. Do not randomly write registers or GPIO.
